  "question": {
    "text": "A man is standing on the platform and one train is approaching and another train is going away with the speed of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, frequency of sound produced by train is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>240</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>. What will be the number of beats heard by him per second? (velocity of sound =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Zero",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The apparent frequency heard by the man is given by<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br />On our case,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br />Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math><br /><br />In the first case, the train is approaching the man, so frequency heard<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>300</mn><mrow><mn>300</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>240</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>296</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>243.24</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math><br /><br />In the second case, the train is going away from the man, so frequency heard<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>240</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>300</mn><mrow><mn>300</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>240</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow><mn>304</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>236.84</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math><br /><br />Hence, the number of beats heard by the man per second<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>243.24</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>236.84</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6.4</mn><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>6</mn></math>"
  }
}